 "captions": {
  "script": "This lake burns skin, and it mummifies the dead. Glitch Diary, entry one. Today I found Lake Natron, in northern Tanzania. Blood red, and only half a meter deep. The water can reach sixty degrees Celsius. Almost as caustic as ammonia. But that's not the strange part. The red isn't blood. It's salt-loving microbes, thriving where little else can. Animals that die on these shores don't rot. They become calcified mummies. And the real glitch? I haven't told you yet. Most of East Africa's lesser flamingos hatch right here. The caustic water is their shield. Predators stay away. A death trap... that works as a nursery. Would you touch this water? Comment below. Follow for the next entry of my glitch diary. Because this lake...",
